  </operand_table>
 <longdesc><para unique="1261278">Adds the single precision floating-point values in the first and second dwords of the destination operand and stores the result in the first dword of the destination operand.</para>
  <para unique="1261279">Adds single precision floating-point values in the third and fourth dword of the destination operand and stores the result in the second dword of the destination operand.</para>
  <para unique="1261280">Adds single precision floating-point values in the first and second dword of the source operand and stores the result in the third dword of the destination operand.</para>
  <para unique="1261281">Adds single precision floating-point values in the third and fourth dword of the source operand and stores the result in the fourth dword of the destination operand. </para>
  <para unique="1261282">In 64-bit mode, use of the REX.R prefix permits this instruction to access additional registers (XMM8-XMM15).</para>
  <para unique="1261286">See <link unique="1261285" linkend="#60346: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 3-11. HADDPS: Packed Single-FP Horizontal Add" xrefstyle="FigureNum">Figure&#160;3&#8209;14</link> for HADDPS; see <link unique="1261289" linkend="#20026: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 3-22. VHADDPS operation" xrefstyle="FigureNum">Figure&#160;3&#8209;15</link> for VHADDPS.</para>
